# Meridiem literals: 12-hour clock readings.
4p
4a
4pm
4:30p
4:30:15pm
11:59:59p
# The two everyone gets wrong.
12a
12p
# `@` with a time keeps the date and replaces the time.
now @ 16:00
now @ 4p
now @ 4a
tomorrow @ 9:15
upcoming friday @ 4p
(now + 1d) @ 17:00
deploy = 2026-07-04T09:00
deploy @ 4p
# It composes with conversion and arithmetic.
now @ 4p in Tokyo
(now @ 16:00) - (now @ 12:00)
now @ 4p + 90m
# `@` with a zone still attaches a zone.
12:13 @ sf
# Errors.
now @ 5h
0p
13p
4:60p
